WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.501
-Our next guest will be touring
Australia this September

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:04.734
with his new show, "Epic."

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.901
Making his
American television debut,

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:10.734
please welcome the very funny
Simon Taylor.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:22.234
-Hello! This is fun.

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:25.167
The last fun thing I did before
I came to America was,

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:28.234
I played "Monopoly"
with my parents.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.167
But they play "Monopoly"
by the modern rules.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.067
Do you know
the modern rules of "Monopoly"?

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:35.667
That's when my parents
start with all the property,

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:38.968
and I just wait for them to die.

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:44.367
Because they're Boomers.
They're so condescending.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:45.501
They're like,
"Well, if you want to get into

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.167
the housing market,
Millennials,

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:51.267
maybe you should stop eating all
that avocado on toast."

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.534
How dare you?

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.634
Let's do the math
for the Boomers, okay?

00:00:55.634 --> 00:01:00.167
25 bucks a pop for
smashed avocado, eggs, coffee.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:02.534
You do that four times a month,
that's 100 bucks a month.

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:04.300
That's 1,200 bucks a year.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.567
So if I want to put a deposit on
a house in an inner-city suburb,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.634
I have to stop eating
avocado toast for

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.968
20 to 30...

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:15.968
thousand years.

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:21.167
There's no way into
the market for my generation.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.534
They don't cater auctions
to Millennials.

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:26.367
There's no auctioneer going,
"Alright, ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.367
welcome to the auction just for
the under 35s here today,

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.267
just for the Millennials here in
the beautiful suburb of

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:34.801
outer, outer Manhattan...

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:35.934
Kansas.

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:38.801
We're in Kansas.
Should have just said that.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.667
We are starting the bidding
on this beautiful

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.133
2"x5" studio apartment.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:49.968
For the under 35s, starting the
bidding today at a job.

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:52.834
Who's got a job?
Does anyone under 35 got a job?

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:53.868
Can I see a job?

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.000
I need a full-time job,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.133
not working part time
in a café, sir.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.000
I can see the tattoos.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.434
I'm looking for savings now.
Does anyone got savings?

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:03.634
Anyone under 35 got savings?
No.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:06.634
Spent it all fixing your
broken phone screen last year.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.400
I'm looking for
rich parents now.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.701
Can I see rich parents?

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:13.167
Going once. Going twice.
Going three times.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:14.934
Sold to the foreign investor."

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.267
It's the best we can hope for.

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:20.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:24.067
You clap, but I'm sad.

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:26.434
I live with
my wonderful partner, Lucy.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:28.968
And living together puts
the relationship to the test.

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:31.367
For example,
Lucy was in bed one night,

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.334
eating cookies
because she'd given up.

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:36.834
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.734
...she had crumbs
all down her front.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.133
And she's like,
"Babe, I can't move.

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:42.267
I don't want to get
crumbs in the bed."

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:46.734
So I vacuumed my girlfriend.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:47.901
And now we're married,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.100
so it all worked out.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.534
I don't deserve that.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:55.767
She proposed to me,
which was pretty cool.

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.567
Any ladies here
propose to the men?

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:58.868
Give us a "yeah."

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.701
That's emasculating. Okay.

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:02.968
It was amazing, right?

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.267
She got down in the
middle of the street, right?

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:08.801
Everyone was walking by, and she
said "Simon, will you marry me?"

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:10.534
And everyone walking by stopped,

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.601
they started
applauding and cheering,

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.934
which made it so hard to say no.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:17.634
And my instinct was like,

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:19.400
"No, no, no,
I was going to get around to it.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.367
I'm transferring money
between accounts.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.701
Give me time."

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:26.534
But as I saw the tears of joy
welling in her eyes,

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:30.033
I realized in that instant
just how much

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.467
money I was going to save.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:35.767
And I said "Yes," right?
Weddings are expensive, man.

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:38.567
Millennials now are
sponsoring their weddings

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:39.868
and putting it on social media

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.801
just to make
some money back, right?

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:45.801
Which I think is so tacky,
and I wish I'd done it.

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:47.634
I would have had
a commercial break

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.367
during the ceremony
if I could have.

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:54.601
Like, "I, Simon, take you, Lucy,
to be my lawful wedded wife.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:58.300
But now,
a quick word from our sponsor.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.801
Going through a divorce
can be tough.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:04.267
That's why Gibson and Power
Divorce Lawyers

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:05.767
are here to help.

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:08.868
Use the promo code
'Till death do us part.'"

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:14.501
Another awkward thing that
happened between Lucy and I was,

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:16.767
one night, we're at the laptop,
and I said,

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:19.133
"Hey, I'm going to
order some food for delivery."

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:24.567
And in front of Lucy, I opened
what's called an incognito tab.

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.534
Some people know what
I'm talking about.

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:27.667
Some people are lost.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.934
For those who don't know,
an incognito tab

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:31.667
is a tab you can open
in your browser

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.801
that doesn't save what
you search to your history.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.834
So you could look up
anything you want, sir,

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.601
and your partner wouldn't know.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:41.100
You're welcome.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.167
Some people knew what it was,
so they giggled.

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.534
Some people didn't know what
an incognito tab was,

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:46.667
so they were quiet.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:49.367
But some people knew what it was
but stayed quiet

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:50.701
because they were thinking,

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.467
"Don't give
away my secret, man.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:55.934
That's my special time."

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.634
So, in front of Lucy,
I've opened an incognito tab,

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:00.901
accidentally,
just, like, out of habit,

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:01.934
because I do it so much.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.400
You know what
I'm talking about, dude.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.734
And she said, "Why did you open
an incognito tab for food?"

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:09.934
And I'm like, "Uh...

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:13.367
I just don't want people knowing
what food I get delivered."

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:15.000
She's like, "What food do you
get delivered?"

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.167
And I panicked and said,
"Interracial.

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:21.868
Fusion. I meant fusion."

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:24.033
My name is Simon Taylor.
Thank you so much!

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:26.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:32.300
-Fusion. Fusion.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.200
Simon Taylor!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.367
Simon Taylor.

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:39.334
He'll be touring Australia
this September.

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:41.300
We'll be right back, everybody.
Come on back.

